ntent": "Accurately use information about travel and vacations in social situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Present Simple Tense vs. The Present Continuous Tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<span class = \"strong\">Simple Present Tense</span><br/><br/>You use the Simple Present tense to talk about:<br/> <span class=\"bullet\"> a routine action or specific action that happens regularly</span><br/> <span class=\"bullet\"> a general truth</span><br/> <span class=\"bullet\"> to give personal information</span><br/><br/>You can use expressions of frequency like every day or always with the Present Simple.<br/><br/><span class = \"strong\">Present Continuous Tense</span><br/><br/>You form the Present Continuous tense with the verb <span class = \"strong\">to be + verb-ing</span>.<br/><br/>You use the Present Continuous tense to talk about:<br/> <span class=\"bullet\"> a current event or action happening around now</span><br/> <span class=\"bullet\"> events that <span class = \"strong\">are going to happen</span> soon (future plans)</span><br/><br/>You can use expressions like right now or later with the Present Continuous."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Some loaves are round. <br/> Bakers here are preparing \"Pan de Muerto,\" the bread of the dead. <br/>  It's good luck to find toys in the bread. <br/>  I am reporting live from the Phoenix Bakery in Cabo San Lucas."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn4le12ob09re2img01.jpg"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "bread "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "food baked in an oven, usually made from wheat"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Bakers are preparing \"Pan de Muerto,\" the bread of the dead."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le12ob09aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about food and holidays."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "listener "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who listens to a radio or TV show"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We wish a happy Dead of the Dead to all of our listeners."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le12ob09aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "shape"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "form"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Many customers come back every year to buy these traditional breads in different shapes."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le12ob09aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "skeleton"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the bones of the human body or other animal"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Bakers are putting plastic toy skeletons in the dough."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le12ob09aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "oven"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "kitchen appliance used for baking"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: As the breads are coming out of the oven, customers are rushing to buy them. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le12ob09aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "plastic"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a hard, light material often used to make small objects"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Did you find a plastic skeleton in the bread?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le12ob09aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "skull "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the bone that protects the human brain"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Some loaves of bread are in the shapes of people, skulls or animals. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le12ob09aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "baker"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who bakes bread or other foods in the oven"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Bakers in Mexico prepare \"Pan de Muerto\"."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le12ob09aud01"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Go online or look in magazines to find images of food that look like different objects. Try to find 10 examples."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look in magazines or go online."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a collage with the images (put them together)."}, {"type": "text", "content": " Present your collage to a teacher or classmate. For each image, say what the food is, and what it looks like."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Explain where the food is from and what is the special occasion."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I identify images of food."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I create a collage."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I describe images and what they represent."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about a special occasion."}]}], "type": "sena"}